# Build output and machine-local wiring. The Android project under gen/ is
# generated by `tauri android init` from tauri.conf.json, so it is reproducible
# and would otherwise add tens of thousands of generated lines to review.
target/
gen/
node_modules/
*.apk
*.aab
*.idsig

# Two files under gen/ are force-added and tracked anyway, because they are
# hand-written source rather than generated output:
#
#   gen/android/app/src/main/java/com/lamtools/sunday/core/MainActivity.kt
#   gen/android/app/src/main/java/com/lamtools/sunday/core/LifecycleBridge.kt
#
# They carry the Activity callbacks. Without them `onStop` never reaches Rust, and a
# `tauri android init` that overwrote them would remove the background signal with no
# diff to review. Forcing them in keeps the ignore rule for the other ~30 generated
# files while making our two edits reviewable.
#
# Known cost: a fresh clone has no gen/ until `tauri android init` runs, and git
# reports these two as deleted until then. Moving them to an overlay directory that
# the build copies in would fix that; it is a build change, not a security one, so it
# is recorded as a follow-up rather than done here.
